# Regression: `Set[int] s = {}` (empty literal) — int-payload cell of the
# Round XXIV Track E axis matrix (companion to
# set_empty_literal_struct_payload.gg + set_empty_literal_string.gg +
# hashset_empty_literal_struct_payload.gg). Pre-fix: same C-emit
# "incompatible types when assigning to type 'GorgetSet' from type 'int32_t'"
# because `infer_collection_element_type` had no `Set__` arm. Scout initially
# thought this passed accidentally at I64_TYPE; pass-1 RE-verified and found
# `Set[int] s = {}` also fails at HEAD.
int main():
    Set[int] s = {}
    s.add(1)
    s.add(2)
    for x in s:
        print(f"{x}")
    return 0
